 API Design – Real-Time Chat System
1. Overview

This document defines the API specifications for a scalable real-time chat system similar to WhatsApp. The system uses a combination of REST APIs for standard operations and WebSocket connections for real-time communication.

2. Base Configuration
Base URL:
https://api.chatapp.com/v1
Authentication:
JSON Web Token (JWT)
Data Format:
JSON
Protocols:
REST (HTTP/HTTPS)
WebSocket (real-time messaging)
3. Authentication APIs
3.1 User Registration

Endpoint:
POST /auth/register

Request Body:

{
  "name": "Ayush Rana",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "password": "hashed_password"
}

Response:

{
  "user_id": "u123",
  "message": "User registered successfully"
}
3.2 User Login

Endpoint:
POST /auth/login

Request Body:

{
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "password": "password"
}

Response:

{
  "token": "JWT_TOKEN",
  "user_id": "u123"
}
4. User APIs
4.1 Get User Profile

Endpoint:
GET /users/{user_id}

Response:

{
  "user_id": "u123",
  "name": "Ayush Rana",
  "phone": "9876543210"
}
4.2 Update User Profile

Endpoint:
PUT /users/{user_id}

Request Body:

{
  "name": "Updated Name"
}
5. Chat APIs
5.1 Create One-to-One Chat

Endpoint:
POST /chats

Request Body:

{
  "participants": ["u123", "u456"],
  "type": "direct"
}

Response:

{
  "chat_id": "c123"
}
5.2 Create Group Chat

Endpoint:
POST /chats/group

Request Body:

{
  "name": "Project Team",
  "participants": ["u123", "u456", "u789"]
}
5.3 Get User Chats

Endpoint:
GET /chats?user_id=u123

6. Message APIs
6.1 Send Message

Endpoint:
POST /messages

Request Body:

{
  "chat_id": "c123",
  "sender_id": "u123",
  "type": "text",
  "content": "Hello",
  "client_msg_id": "msg_temp_001"
}

Response:

{
  "message_id": "m123",
  "status": "sent"
}
6.2 Retrieve Messages (Pagination)

Endpoint:
GET /messages?chat_id=c123&limit=20&cursor=abc123

Response:

{
  "messages": [],
  "next_cursor": "xyz456"
}
6.3 Update Message Status

Endpoint:
PATCH /messages/{message_id}/status

Request Body:

{
  "status": "read"
}
6.4 Delete Message

Endpoint:
DELETE /messages/{message_id}

7. Media APIs
7.1 Upload Media

Endpoint:
POST /media/upload

Response:

{
  "media_url": "https://storage.service/file.jpg"
}
7.2 Send Media Message

Example Payload:

{
  "chat_id": "c123",
  "type": "image",
  "media_url": "https://storage.service/file.jpg"
}
8. Notification APIs (Internal Use)
8.1 Send Notification

Endpoint:
POST /notifications/send

9. WebSocket API (Real-Time Communication)
9.1 Connection

Endpoint:
ws://api.chatapp.com/ws?token=JWT_TOKEN

9.2 Events
Send Message Event
{
  "event": "send_message",
  "data": {
    "chat_id": "c123",
    "content": "Hello"
  }
}
Receive Message Event
{
  "event": "new_message",
  "data": {
    "message_id": "m123",
    "sender_id": "u456",
    "content": "Hi"
  }
}
Typing Indicator
{
  "event": "typing",
  "chat_id": "c123"
}
Read Receipt
{
  "event": "read_receipt",
  "message_id": "m123"
}
10. Design Considerations
Idempotency:
client_msg_id ensures duplicate message prevention.
Pagination:
Cursor-based pagination improves performance for large datasets.
Security:
HTTPS for all communication
JWT-based authentication
Optional end-to-end encryption
Rate Limiting:
Applied to prevent abuse and ensure system stability.
